  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Here's one of the most powerful arrangements in modern finance, hiding in plain sight. Nearly all the world's oil is priced in US dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "globe",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "globe"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Oil = dollars.",
            "The weapon."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Think about what that forces. If almost every country must buy oil, then almost every country must first hold dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "globe",
          "kicker": "why it matters",
          "line": "Everyone needs dollars",
          "sub": "to buy the oil they run on"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Oil exporters then recycle those dollars back into US assets.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-petro",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · petrodollar recycling"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That creates a permanent, worldwide demand for dollars that no other country enjoys.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "always-on",
          "label": "global demand for dollars",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "bill"
          ]
